From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:37:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 106/148] hjviewer: an own PC's close button shows when it
 locks, and its screen hides on connect (TV-W3)

TV-W3, controller side (design build/v19/design/w3-w4.md 3-2, 3-3, 5-3,
5-4; decisions D-9 and D-10; critic X-11, X-19, C-09). Rules and texts
in the new flutter/lib/common/hjviewer_end_lock.dart (pure), the session
screen wiring in hjviewer_end_lock_ui.dart, the Rust in the new child
module src/client/hjv_end_lock.rs; upstream files get thin hooks.

- Mode: an own PC (the PC sent platform_additions.hjv_end_lock) keeps
  automatic / always / never in PeerConfig hjv-end-lock (empty =
  automatic). Desktop: the Display menu's submenu 'Lock this PC when
  the session ends'; phone: a radio group in the display options. The
  choice goes as sessionToggleOption 'hjv-end-lock:<mode>', which sends
  OptionMessage.hjv_end_lock with the upstream field (Yes only for
  always) and keeps the upstream flag true only for always; the login
  carries the kept mode (pinned builds). Other PCs and 1.8.x PCs keep
  upstream's 'Lock after session end', which now drops a kept mode.
- Lock mark: the desktop toolbar's close and the phone's disconnect
  button carry a 10 px lock, and their tooltip and name say the PC
  locks, only when it will for sure: always, or automatic and the PC
  was locked at the start; never in view-only mode or without keyboard
  permission. Not on the tab or window close (X-11). The phone's close
  confirmation adds 'The PC locks when you end the session.'
- Hide on connect: an own PC's 'Hide the screen when connecting'
  (PeerConfig hjv-hide-on-connect, default off) turns privacy mode on
  after the first image; upstream's re-enable from the last session's
  state is off for every PC in pinned builds (D-10). Greyed when the PC
  does not allow privacy mode. A failure of that attempt is one toast
  per session instead of the box (D9; a failure by hand stays a box).
- X-19: the phone's switch to the same PC's file transfer sends a
  one-off never ('hjv-end-lock-once:never', not kept) before it closes
  the remote screen, so the switch does not lock the PC. The PC now
  forgets a session key's "locked at the start" only after an end that
  locked, so the screen the phone comes back to (same session ID)
  inherits it and locks at its own end.

Tests: client::hjv_end_lock (mode choice and the fields sent, the
one-off never, upstream's switch, the login option, hide on connect
pinned and unpinned); flutter/test/hjviewer_end_lock_test.dart (mode,
lock mark, quiet failure, texts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
